  "body": "### Summary\nAs a dark-mode user, I want the Fête nationale fireworks and bust to keep a visible halo, so that the dark outlines of the art do not vanish into the dark background (WCAG 1.4.11, THEMES.md §4 rule 7).\n\n### Scope\n`FeteNationaleScene` (LOT-194, #1438) draws its bursts with a single `.shadow(color: .white.opacity(0.85), radius: 1.5)` on a dark scheme. LOT-191 (#1441) rendered that same shadow with `ImageRenderer` at 3x over the dark `#121014` with a purple edge: going outward from the edge, the halo's contrast against the background is 3.7, 2.9, 2.2, 1.8 per device pixel, so it is at least 3:1 over about 0.33 pt only. The same shadow stacked twice (`.shadow(…).shadow(…)`) measures 10.9, 8.8, 6.9, 5.1, 3.7, at least 3:1 over about 1.7 pt. The Fête numbers over its own black background were not rendered; the shadow parameters are the same, so they should be close.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- On a dark scheme the burst art keeps a halo at least 3:1 against the background over at least 1.5 pt.\n- A test renders the burst sprite (`ImageRenderer`, 3x, dark background) and measures the pixels next to the art; it fails with the single shadow. `SamainDecorationTests` in #1441 (`theRenderedRimKeepsEveryImagesSilhouetteThreeToOneOnTheDarkBackground`) is a model.\n\nNot changed in #1441: Fête is LOT-194's.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
